{"title":"Inner product","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>For a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vector_space\" title=\"Vector space\">vector space</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/7876671d1a34e42c976a8c88802554c9b286ae2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle V$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875c16036f2c2c65cabad177d7908d0d6aac986c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F \\subseteq \\mathbb{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />), an <b>inner product</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binary_operation\" title=\"Binary operation\">binary operation</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/91493a4c59d2a31ab2766693331f4ac1d1d78bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle : V \\times V \\mapsto \\mathbb{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" /> (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />) which satisfies the following axioms:\n</p>\n<ul><li>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11974b91ff1b8f0ac5dd86f7fd8f3c0651bcdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{v, w} \\in V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/8/c08ce9afd1eb4ef5c6d0b5131af3aab4f890e9e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{ v,w } \\rangle = \\overline{ \\langle \\mathbf{ w,v } \\rangle }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"22\" />.</li>\n<li>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076eba6175bf40436ca7a4b104f614a8e92f7250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha \\in F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/4153bd8bd552ba4a4aecf465435579f5a30b792e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{v,w} \\in V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ecb34426e23b48cd9c4074ec5185ad43ee3db5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\alpha \\mathbf{v,w} \\rangle = \\alpha\\langle \\mathbf{v,w} \\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"19\" />.</li>\n<li>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/9/dc9b72e0e9569a71f9833f914bf1ae1d51f43b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{u,v,w} \\in V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c29a27c3d417b1e2153117cf32dea40ccd20e617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{ u+v, w} \\rangle = \\langle \\mathbf{u,w} \\rangle + \\langle \\mathbf{ v, w } \\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"226\" height=\"19\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>From these three axioms we can also conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20bc777b9a80ece0b0382fd08e1d80006ae4f97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{v}, \\alpha\\mathbf{w} \\rangle = \\alpha \\langle \\mathbf{v,w} \\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a4150421e4df24e51390cb945757211e49660add.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{ v, u+w} \\rangle = \\langle \\mathbf{v,u} \\rangle + \\langle \\mathbf{v,w} \\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21a35b83482738859a6641316c01830a0b1c8104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{v} \\in V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f0f62caedb4486ca07b6afebcb6a7fe104e1f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{v, v} \\rangle \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />, with equality if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a740ea49e87b1bd420474f8fea22d291cdaa99d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{0}$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>This is reasonable because from the first axiom, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a991fbca660c794541dc4a1e17d670a6fc0a6ea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{v,v} \\rangle \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Note that from these axioms we may also obtain the following result:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65ef08ce03a4981dbdd7cb5f14dcafa578834eba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{v,w} \\rangle = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce953b917ec5b9f120ce9c26c64e6e3483aba2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{w}\\in V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a1051d60007c63dc30597067efbd34cf7cc1d09e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{v = 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>This is occasionally listed as an axiom in place of the condition that equality holds on the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aaef5009f0906839b155b5cf7f36e06742e8b973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle \\mathbf{v,v} \\rangle = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> exactly when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddef12714dfa3fc26632d68cecc95e13b45ff73c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{v=0}$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inner_product&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the vector space <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/359c93f77ee9ad4fdfaae8b7c46a2d7ed91a3b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}^n$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dot_product\" title=\"Dot product\">dot product</a> is perhaps the most familiar example of an inner product.\n</p><p>In addition, for the vector space <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734ef645c78704dbe5a136258a49d8425298f623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" /> of continuous functions mapping some interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443630b21df9a161a719e6463669aae4219b6b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I \\mapsto \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, the operator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc179cc4b48b071bf18bce04e9683ad87f77d69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\int_{I} f(x)g(x) dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"109\" height=\"40\" /> is an inner product for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cfcbc061a3adb9d87307cdf197726dca2844ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f, g \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inner_product&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</a></li></ul>\n<p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Inner_product&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018091359\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 155/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 280/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5491/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.930      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.930      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4875:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018091359 and revision id 14563. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}